    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50412" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμαλίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, Syrac. epith. of Demeter, <i><span class="en">
			Polem.
		</span></i> Hist.<i><span class="en">
			39
		</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμαλιά</span></b> , ἡ,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ
			ἐπίμετρον τῶν ἀλεύρων</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάλιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abundant</i>, Id.: as name of a
			month at Hierapytna, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5040.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Dor.
			 word for 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ νόστος καὶ τὰ ἐπίμετρα τῶν
					ἀλεύρων</span>”
